        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-11955",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{-2}{4x-9}$, find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=-2$ and $v(x)=4x-9,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{\u2032}(x) & =0, \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}(x) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x){v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0)\\cdot (4x-9)-(-2)\\cdot (4)}{{(4x-9)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{(4x-9)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
