        ":question/id": "2d5c94d4-600d-5879-b9be-f30602b81bb7",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104305",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{10}{3-{x}^{2}}$, find ${f}^{'}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=10$ and $v(x)=3-{x}^{2},$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{'}(x) & =0, \\\\ {v}^{'}(x) & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0)\\cdot (3-{x}^{2})-(10)\\cdot (-2x)}{{(3-{x}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{20x}{{(3-{x}^{2})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      {
