        ":question/id": "ecceb386-fdf1-5dd9-81d5-114b41a2975b",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-128235",
        ":question/problem": "Find the derivative of $f(x).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${f}^{\u2032}(x)\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=x-2$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}+4x+k,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{\u2032}(x) & =1, \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}(x) & =2x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)({x}^{2}+4x+k)-(x-2)(2x+4)}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+4x+k)-(2{x}^{2}-8)}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-{x}^{2}+4x+k+8}{{({x}^{2}+4x+k)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      {
