        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{6x}{1-3x}$, find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=6x$ and $v(x)=1-3x,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{\u2032}(x) & =6, \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}(x) & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{\u2032}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{\u2032}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot (1-3x)-6x\\cdot (-3)}{{(1-3x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-18x+18x}{{(1-3x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{(1-3x)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
